w00t Omgrofl (Juraj Borza, 2006): a language made of chat abbreviations.
w00t Its variables are lol, lool, loool and so on, with as many o as you
w00t like, and its words say what they do, more or less:
w00t   lol iz 73        lol takes the value 73
w00t   rofl lol         prints lol as a character (73 is I)
w00t   lmao lol         adds one to lol, roflmao takes one away
w00t   w00t             starts a comment, like this line
w00t   stfu             ends the program
w00t Run it with the Omgrofl interpreter: omgrofl hello.omgrofl
w00t It prints, letter by letter:

w00t I
lol iz 73
rofl lol
w00t a space
lool iz 32
rofl lool
w00t give
loool iz 103
rofl loool
lol iz 105
rofl lol
lool iz 118
rofl lool
loool iz 101
rofl loool
w00t a space
lol iz 32
rofl lol
w00t you
lool iz 121
rofl lool
loool iz 111
rofl loool
lol iz 117
rofl lol
w00t a space
lool iz 32
rofl lool
w00t a
loool iz 97
rofl loool
w00t a space
rofl lool
w00t rendez-vous
lol iz 114
